  </p>
  <p>
    The <strong>Global Positioning System (GPS)</strong>—formally known as NAVSTAR GPS—is the world's most pervasive positioning utility. In this comprehensive guide, we unpack the mathematical principles, physical phenomena, and computational algorithms that transform orbital radio transmissions into sub-meter coordinates on your screen.
  </p>

